+# OpenRASP Secondary Development Version
+
+This repository is a secondary development based on the [Baidu OpenRASP](https://github.com/baidu/openrasp.git) open-source project. It enhances detection capabilities, extends the cloud control backend, and optimizes deployment methods on top of the original core functionality.
+
+---
+
+## Original Project Documentation
+
+- [Original English README](README_origin.md)
+- [Original Chinese README](README_CN_origin.md)
+
+## Reference Repository
+
+```
+https://github.com/baidu/openrasp.git
+```
+
+---
+
+## Secondary Development Features
+
+### 1. Java Agent Detection Logic Enhancement
+
+#### 1.1 File Write Event Content Extraction
+
+In the `FileOutputStreamHook` detection point, a new feature has been added to read and extract the content of files being written. When a file write event is triggered, the system attempts to read the target file content (up to 4 KB) and reports it along with the event parameters to facilitate subsequent security analysis. To avoid circular triggering with the `FileInputStreamHook` read file detection, a `ThreadLocal` context marking mechanism is introduced to ensure that the content extraction process does not repeatedly trigger read file detection events.
+
+#### 1.2 Event Field Name Desensitization
+
+Field names related to attack behavior in event logs have been adjusted to more neutral expressions to accommodate log specification requirements in different scenarios:
+
+| Original Field Name | Adjusted Field Name |
+|---------------------|---------------------|
+| `attack_params` | `raw_behavior_params` |
+| `attack_type` | `raw_behavior` |
+| `attack_source` | `request_source` |
+
+The above field renaming takes effect only when `event_type` is `record_log`; other event types remain unchanged.
+
+### 2. Detection Plugin Enhancement
+
+Based on the official JavaScript plugin, multiple rounds of iterative optimization have been performed for the file write (`writefile`) detection scenario. The plugin is located at `openrasp/plugins/official/plugin-v3`:
+
+- **plugin-v3**: Adjusted the writefile script file detection logic, suppressed original event reporting, fixed the issue where uploaded scripts did not trigger events, and eliminated false positives caused by `.so` file writes.
+
+### 3. Cloud Control Backend (rasp-cloud) Extension
+
+#### 3.1 Base64 Escaping Fix
+
+Fixed an issue where the Base64 encoded character `+` was incorrectly escaped in the cloud control backend, ensuring data integrity involving special characters during transmission and storage.
+
+### 4. Docker Deployment Support
+
+A complete `rasp-cloud-docker` build directory has been added, providing a containerized deployment solution based on Alpine 3.18. The directory includes a Dockerfile, frontend static resources, backend binary files, configuration files, a GeoIP database, and email/crash report templates, enabling one-click containerized build and deployment of the cloud control management backend.
+
+### 5. Compilation Adaptation
+
+The Java compilation target version has been adjusted from 1.6 to 1.8, resolving compilation failures in high-version JDK environments (e.g., JDK 18) and ensuring the project can be built successfully in modern Java environments.
+
+---
+
+## Build Instructions
+
+### OpenRASP Java Agent Build
+
+Execute the following command in the project root directory:
+
+```bash
+./build-java.sh
+```
+
+After a successful build, the following installation packages will be generated in the project root directory:
+
+- `rasp-java.tar.gz` — Installation package for Linux / macOS
+- `rasp-java.zip` — Installation package for Windows
+
+> **Note**: If the compilation environment uses JDK 12 or higher, ensure that the `source` and `target` versions in `pom.xml` are set to 1.8 or higher. This repository has already made the necessary adaptation adjustments.
+
+---
+
+## OpenRASP Cloud Management Backend
+
+### Image Build
+
+Enter the `rasp-cloud-docker` directory and execute the following command to build the Docker image:
+
+```bash
+cd rasp-cloud-docker
+docker build -t rasp-cloud:latest .
+```
+
+> **Tip**: If network access failures occur during the build (e.g., `apk add` cannot connect to the Alpine package repository), proxy parameters can be passed via `--build-arg`:
+>
+> ```bash
+> docker build \
+>   --build-arg HTTP_PROXY=http://<proxy-ip:port> \
+>   --build-arg HTTPS_PROXY=http://<proxy-ip:port> \
+>   -t rasp-cloud:latest .
+> ```
+
+### Image Run
+
+The cloud control management backend depends on MongoDB and Elasticsearch components. Below is a recommended `docker-compose.yml` configuration example:
+
+```yaml
+version: "3.8"
+
+services:
+  mongodb:
+    image: mongo:4.4
+    container_name: mongodb
+    networks:
+      - rasp-net
+    restart: unless-stopped
+
+  elasticsearch:
+    image: elasticsearch:6.8.23
+    container_name: es
+    ports:
+      - "9201:9200"
+    networks:
+      - rasp-net
+    environment:
+      - discovery.type=single-node
+    ulimits:
+      memlock:
+        soft: -1
+        hard: -1
+    volumes:
+      - es-data:/usr/share/elasticsearch/data
+    healthcheck:
+      test: ["CMD-SHELL", "curl -s -f http://localhost:9200/_cluster/health || exit 1"]
+      interval: 5s
+      timeout: 3s
+      retries: 30
+    restart: unless-stopped
+
+  rasp-cloud:
+    image: rasp-cloud:latest
+    container_name: rasp-cloud
+    dns_search: .
+    dns: 127.0.0.11
+    networks:
+      - rasp-net
+      - kafka-net
+    ports:
+      - "8086:8086"
+    depends_on:
+      mongodb:
+        condition: service_started
+      elasticsearch:
+        condition: service_healthy
+    volumes:
+      - ./resources/rasp-cloud/app.conf:/app/conf/app.conf
+    restart: unless-stopped
+
+networks:
+  rasp-net:
+  kafka-net:
+
+volumes:
+  es-data:
+```
+
+#### Parameter Configuration Description
+
+| Configuration Item | Description |
+|-------------------|-------------|
+| `mongodb` | Uses the MongoDB 4.4 image as the data storage service for the cloud control backend |
+| `elasticsearch` | Uses the Elasticsearch 6.8.23 image as the log retrieval and data analysis engine; externally maps port `9201` (host) → `9200` (container) to avoid conflicts with existing ES instances on the host; ensures `rasp-cloud` starts only after the service is ready via `healthcheck` |
+| `rasp-cloud` | Uses the `rasp-cloud:latest` image built above; exposes port `8086`; controls startup order via `depends_on` to ensure MongoDB and Elasticsearch are ready before starting; mounts `app.conf` for external configuration injection |
+| `volumes` | Mounts the host `./resources/rasp-cloud/app.conf` to `/app/conf/app.conf` in the container to facilitate configuration adjustments without rebuilding the image |
+| `networks` | `rasp-net` is used for internal cloud control component communication; `kafka-net` is used for integration with external Kafka message queues (if Kafka log reporting is required) |
+| `restart` | Uniformly set to `unless-stopped` to ensure automatic recovery after abnormal service exits |
+
+> **Note**: Please ensure SELinux is disabled on the host before starting to avoid permission issues when container volumes are mounted.
+
+#### Plugin Enablement
+
+After the management backend installation is complete, you need to upload the `plugin-v3.js` plugin via the management backend client page. Log in to the cloud control backend, navigate to `Plugin Management → Select Plugin → Submit` to perform the upload operation. After the upload is complete, select the push operation from the action bar.
+
+---
+
+## OpenRASP Java Agent Probe Installation
+
+For specific Java application probe installation methods, please refer to the official documentation:
+
+[https://rasp.baidu.com/doc/install/manual/tomcat.html#auto](https://rasp.baidu.com/doc/install/manual/tomcat.html#auto)
+
+### Prerequisites
+
+Before installing the probe, the cloud control management backend must be deployed first, and the following three key parameters must be obtained:
+
+- `app_id`
+- `app_secret`
+- `backend_url`
+
+These parameters are used for probe registration and communication with the cloud control backend. The probe cannot be properly connected if any of these parameters is missing.
+
