+## Project Architecture Overview
+
+This project consists of two core components, each serving a distinct purpose:
+
+**OpenRASP Cloud Management Backend**: Responsible for receiving, storing, and analyzing security event data reported by the Java Agent. It provides a Web management interface for policy configuration, plugin management, alert viewing, and unified management of multiple applications. The backend depends on MongoDB for application and configuration storage, and on Elasticsearch for log retrieval and data analysis.
+
+**OpenRASP Java Agent Probe**: Deployed on the Tomcat server hosting the Java application to be protected. It uses Java Instrumentation technology to perform Hook detection on sensitive functions at runtime (such as file writes, database queries, and command execution). When abnormal behavior is detected, the Agent reports event information to the management backend in real time and decides whether to block the current request based on the configured policy.
+
+### Data Flow Process
+
+The following diagram illustrates the complete data flow of the OpenRASP Java Agent probe within the system:
+
+```
++-------------------+     Hook Detection    +----------------------+
+|   Application     | ------------------->  |  OpenRASP Java Agent |
+|    (Tomcat)       |                       |       Probe          |
+|                   | <-------------------  |                      |
+|                   |   Block / Allow       |   Capture Events     |
++-------------------+                       +----------+-----------+
+                                                       |
+                                                       | Write Logs
+                                                       v
+                                            +---------------------+
+                                            |  OpenRASP Event      |
+                                            |  Log Files           |
+                                            |  (rasp/logs)         |
+                                            +----------+----------+
+                                                       |
+                                                       | Collect
+                                                       v
+                                            +---------------------+
+                                            |      Filebeat        |
+                                            |   (Read Log Files)   |
+                                            +----------+----------+
+                                                       |
+                                                       | Forward
+                                                       v
+                                            +---------------------+
+                                            |      Logstash        |
+                                            +----------+----------+
+                                                       |
+                            +--------------------------+--------------------------+
+                            |                                                     |
+                            | Push                                                | Push
+                            v                                                     v
+                +---------------------+                               +---------------------+
+                |       Kafka         |                               |   Elasticsearch     |
+                | (For baseline       |                               |   (For ai-agent     |
+                |  and ai-agent       |                               |    analysis)        |
+                |  analysis)          |                               |                     |
+                +---------------------+                               +---------------------+
+```
+
+Process Description:
+
+1. **Event Capture**: At runtime, the OpenRASP Agent intercepts sensitive function calls via Hook technology and captures abnormal behavior events.
+2. **Log Persistence**: The Agent writes abnormal events to local log files (default location: `rasp/logs` directory).
+3. **Log Collection**: Filebeat continuously monitors the log directory and collects newly generated event log data in real time.
+4. **Data Distribution**: Filebeat forwards the collected data to Logstash, which performs data parsing and routing.
+5. **Downstream Push**: Logstash simultaneously pushes event data to two downstream components:
+   - **Kafka**: Provides a real-time data stream for baseline analysis and AI-Agent analysis.
+   - **Elasticsearch**: Provides structured data storage and retrieval capabilities for AI-Agent analysis.
+
+---
+
 ## Secondary Development Features
 
 ### 1. Java Agent Detection Logic Enhancement
@@ -169,7 +234,7 @@ volumes:
 | `mongodb` | Uses the MongoDB 4.4 image as the data storage service for the cloud control backend |
 | `elasticsearch` | Uses the Elasticsearch 6.8.23 image as the log retrieval and data analysis engine; externally maps port `9201` (host) → `9200` (container) to avoid conflicts with existing ES instances on the host; ensures `rasp-cloud` starts only after the service is ready via `healthcheck` |
 | `rasp-cloud` | Uses the `rasp-cloud:latest` image built above; exposes port `8086`; controls startup order via `depends_on` to ensure MongoDB and Elasticsearch are ready before starting; mounts `app.conf` for external configuration injection |
-| `volumes` | Mounts the host `./resources/rasp-cloud/app.conf` to `/app/conf/app.conf` in the container to facilitate configuration adjustments without rebuilding the image |
+| `volumes` | Mounts the host `./resources/rasp-cloud/app.conf` (replace the path according to your actual environment) to `/app/conf/app.conf` in the container to facilitate configuration adjustments without rebuilding the image |
 | `networks` | `rasp-net` is used for internal cloud control component communication; `kafka-net` is used for integration with external Kafka message queues (if Kafka log reporting is required) |
 | `restart` | Uniformly set to `unless-stopped` to ensure automatic recovery after abnormal service exits |
 
