-## Project Architecture Overview
-
 This project consists of two core components, each serving a distinct purpose:
 
 **OpenRASP Cloud Management Backend**: Responsible for receiving, storing, and analyzing security event data reported by the Java Agent. It provides a Web management interface for policy configuration, plugin management, alert viewing, and unified management of multiple applications. The backend depends on MongoDB for application and configuration storage, and on Elasticsearch for log retrieval and data analysis.
 
-**OpenRASP Java Agent Probe**: Deployed on the Tomcat server hosting the Java application to be protected. It uses Java Instrumentation technology to perform Hook detection on sensitive functions at runtime (such as file writes, database queries, and command execution). When abnormal behavior is detected, the Agent reports event information to the management backend in real time and decides whether to block the current request based on the configured policy.
-
-## Data Flow Process
+**OpenRASP Java Agent Telemetry Source**: Deployed on the Java application server to be protected. It uses Java Instrumentation technology to perform Hook detection on sensitive functions at runtime (such as file writes, database queries, and command execution). When abnormal behavior is detected, the Agent reports event information to the management backend in real time and decides whether to block the current request based on the configured policy.
 
